floating-comparison-builtins.c:
  All four oracle compile/run pairs exit 0.
  Subject --interpret-c-hir: E2001, undeclared __builtin_isless, line 8.
  Covers the six comparison builtins, mixed arithmetic operands, NaN, signed
  zero, and exactly-once operand evaluation. No strict-fenv claim.
  Original affected LLVM files: ieee/compare-fp-{1,3,4}.c and ieee/pr50310.c.

polynomial-scalar-place.c (actual target arm_neon.h):
  All four oracle compile/run pairs exit 0.
  Subject --interpret-c-hir with all three shared sysroot include directories:
  E2101, expected-modifiable-lvalue at got = bytes[0], line 15.
  Final controls include all four polynomial scalar widths, including 128.
  Original: UnitTests/Vector/AArch64/aarch64_neon_intrinsics.c:72230.
  This is a polynomial scalar place defect, not a floating-vector deferral.

static-narrow-member-offset.c:
  Same four oracle compile/run pairs (without -ffp-contract=off) exit 0.
  Subject C-HIR: E3009 null-pointer-access, line 7.
  Subject EvoIR lowering: E3101 global initializer is not an admitted integer
  constant at that initializer. No object is read by this address calculation.
  Final controls also retain the intermediate unsigned-char truncation of
  a 264-byte field offset; both oracles still compile/run 0 at O0/O2.
  Original: TinyCC libtcc.c:1709, options_W's unsigned-short offset field.
  This does not authorize runtime null dereferences or symbolic address guesses.

These are RED observations against the frozen binary, not repaired results.

floating-environment-dominance.c and its reference-built driver:
  Both oracles at O0/O2 with -ffp-contract=off compile/run 0 on the value tests.
  The frozen subject also passes those values and the driver's CHECK_ADMISSION
  mode: post-call FPCR mutation and each branch of one() still produce SIGTRAP;
  transport preserves foreign FPCR. This is a semantic control, not a RED.
  The performance RED is the emitted admission count per function:
    chain=3, loop=3, both=3; required after dominance reuse: 1, 1, 2.
    one=2, after_call=2, after_asm=2, after_asm_goto=2, transport=0 must stay so.
  No full benchmark runtime improvement is inferred from these counts.

